WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.340
You've come out with an album?

00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:02.500
I have, I have.

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:03.960
Well the Muppets and
I went into the studio

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:06.160
to do this album, we sort of got lost.

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:08.050
Ended up singing with a lot of people

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:09.030
and it made a nice album,

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:10.800
so we put it all together, lot's of fun.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.288
Yeah, well I was gonna ask you about this.

00:00:12.288 --> 00:00:13.493
(audience laughs)

00:00:13.493 --> 00:00:16.010
This is very risky,
very risky when actors,

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:17.970
when actors try and sing.

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:19.730
You know, Telly Savalas tried it.

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:20.720
What, you're kidding.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.140
Yeah, William Shatner.

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:22.973
(audience laughs)

00:00:22.973 --> 00:00:23.806
Wow.

00:00:23.806 --> 00:00:24.639
William Shatner tried it.

00:00:24.639 --> 00:00:25.610
A lot of people, Leonard Nimoy,

00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:27.600
I think all of the Star
Trek cast has tried it.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:28.433
Gee.

00:00:28.433 --> 00:00:29.950
Yeah, it's very risky.

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:31.630
Yeah, well it can be risky, sure.

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:34.150
But I've actually been singing for years.

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:36.520
I'm kind of known as a
singer, as well as, and actor.

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:38.150
It's kind of a frog thing.

00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:39.130
Go to the swamp sometime.

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:40.010
You'll hear us singing.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:41.500
I didn't realize that about you.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:42.333
You're so talented.

00:00:42.333 --> 00:00:43.440
Well, that's very nice of you.

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:44.560
Yeah, nothing really.

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:45.393
Nothing really.

00:00:45.393 --> 00:00:47.420
Now, I understand (audience laughs)

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:48.407
in part of this you're,

00:00:48.407 --> 00:00:49.770
and part of some, you're actually singing

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:50.960
with Ozzy Osbourne?

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:53.360
Well actually, yes that's true.

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:54.193
That's true.

00:00:54.193 --> 00:00:55.026
Ozzy was around.

00:00:55.026 --> 00:00:56.900
Miss Piggy actually sung with Ozzy.

00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:57.733
Miss Piggy--

00:00:57.733 --> 00:00:58.710
Oh, Miss Piggy does.

00:00:58.710 --> 00:00:59.730
Yeah, it's very interesting.

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:01.598
Ozzy has a way with barnyard animals.

00:01:01.598 --> 00:01:03.355
(audience loudly laughs)

00:01:03.355 --> 00:01:04.188
Yeah, I don't know.

00:01:04.188 --> 00:01:05.021
It's true.

00:01:05.021 --> 00:01:07.250
(audience claps)

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:08.690
Who knew, who knew?

00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:09.523
That's true.

00:01:09.523 --> 00:01:10.660
Now, I worked on the,

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:11.560
I worked on the,

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:12.940
I was asked to be in the video.

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:14.800
I guess you got a lot
of people in the video.

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:15.633
We did.

00:01:15.633 --> 00:01:17.630
We got a whole long list
of big celebrities, yeah.

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:18.463
Yes, thank you.

00:01:18.463 --> 00:01:19.410
And you were great by the way.

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:20.243
Oh, thank you very much.

00:01:20.243 --> 00:01:21.670
A little thing I do.

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:23.140
But I was curious about this.

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:26.360
I was back stage there and I sensed

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:28.317
that there was a lot
of tension back stage.

00:01:28.317 --> 00:01:31.270
Oh, oh you mean like
lots of egos and stuff.

00:01:31.270 --> 00:01:32.103
Yeah.

00:01:32.103 --> 00:01:33.990
It seemed like a lot of
you guys were very tense

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:36.990
and you sort of, success
has gone to your head.

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:38.950
Yeah, it happens sometimes.

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:40.610
But a lot of that was Miss Piggy.

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:43.420
We told people to just check
their egos at the door,

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:46.064
but we couldn't find a check
room large enough for Piggy.

00:01:46.064 --> 00:01:47.272
(audience laughs)

00:01:47.272 --> 00:01:49.970
She can instigate a lot of
problems with big stars.

00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:52.770
Now, speaking of her, are
you still an item with her?

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:53.750
Are you guys still going out?

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:54.773
An item?

00:01:54.773 --> 00:01:55.993
Yeah, are you still going
out with Miss Piggy?

00:01:55.993 --> 00:01:58.590
No, no Conan, I believe
you have been misinformed.

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:01.260
You see, may I take this
opportunity on national television

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:02.990
to say folks, that there is nothing,

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:04.337
nothing going on between Piggy and I

00:02:04.337 --> 00:02:07.130
other than a purely
professional relationship.

00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:07.963
Ah.

00:02:07.963 --> 00:02:08.796
No, no, please.

00:02:08.796 --> 00:02:09.730
Really, really?

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:10.930
A lot of us were misled.

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:12.910
Well, I think that has
a lot do with Miss Piggy

00:02:12.910 --> 00:02:15.240
being able to fax her
press releases directly

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:16.401
to the "National Enquirer."

00:02:16.401 --> 00:02:17.512
(audience laughs)

00:02:17.512 --> 00:02:18.360
I see.

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:19.470
Now, let me ask you something.

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:20.510
Who is she involved with?

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:21.810
Is she seeing anybody right now?

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:24.450
Well there is, and this
is only a rumor, mind you,

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:26.440
but I hear that she has
been seen around town

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:27.273
with Tom Arnold.

00:02:27.273 --> 00:02:29.023
(audience loudly laughs)

00:02:29.023 --> 00:02:29.856
Yeah.

00:02:32.214 --> 00:02:33.290
You heard it here, folks.

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:35.400
Yeah, but who am I to mind, you know?

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:36.590
I would not mind.

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:37.610
I would not mind at all.

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:38.920
She can do whatever she likes.

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:40.190
It's okay with me.

00:02:40.190 --> 00:02:41.080
I don't care.

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:41.913
It's okay.

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:44.021
She's a pig, what can I say?

00:02:44.021 --> 00:02:45.330
(Conan and audience laughs)

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:47.350
I'll let you (laughs).

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:50.490
Oh, it's the 90's now.

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:51.710
Women can do whatever they want.

00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:53.330
Sure, and they can even be pigs.

00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:54.163
Yes.

00:02:54.163 --> 00:02:55.040
Nothing personal.

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:56.190
I don't wanna get letters.

00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:58.440
No, you're not gonna
get no letters at all.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:02:59.410
No letters at all.

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:00.700
Kermit, let me ask you.

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:02.660
I know that you did,

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:04.610
you substituted for Johnny Carson once.

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:05.443
That's true.

00:03:05.443 --> 00:03:08.330
And you actually sat in
for, was it Larry King?

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:09.560
I did do that one time, yes.

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:10.393
Not so long ago?

00:03:10.393 --> 00:03:11.226
I was great fun.

00:03:11.226 --> 00:03:12.230
Yeah, well you've actually,

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:13.820
so then you've had quite a bit experience

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:14.653
with this talk show thing.

00:03:14.653 --> 00:03:17.520
Have you ever, ever considered
doing your own talk show?

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:19.190
Well, I suppose

00:03:19.190 --> 00:03:21.150
if the opportunity
presented itself, maybe.

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:22.390
I've been told that I look sort of

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:24.369
like a short green Regis Philbin.

00:03:24.369 --> 00:03:26.350
(audience laughs)

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:27.333
Yeah, yeah?

00:03:28.711 --> 00:03:29.544
But I don't know.

00:03:29.544 --> 00:03:30.377
I can see it, I can see it.

00:03:30.377 --> 00:03:31.300
Yeah, maybe, maybe.

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:32.800
It was fun doing the Larry King thing.

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:33.830
It's kinda scary though.

00:03:33.830 --> 00:03:35.470
You know, it goes, I mean
you do this every night

00:03:35.470 --> 00:03:37.809
but I'm just kind of a simple frog.

00:03:37.809 --> 00:03:38.642
You know, I just--

00:03:38.642 --> 00:03:39.475
No, but you seem to do it well.

00:03:39.475 --> 00:03:40.740
You're a very good conversationalist.

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:41.573
Well, I don't know--

00:03:41.573 --> 00:03:42.406
C'mon, you are.

00:03:42.406 --> 00:03:43.780
Well okay, all right, maybe I am.

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:45.100
Maybe I should give it a try sometime.

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:45.986
What do you think, huh?

00:03:45.986 --> 00:03:47.971
(audience claps)

00:03:47.971 --> 00:03:49.330
Everyone has a show now.

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:50.220
You should have a show.

00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:51.367
Well, thank you.

00:03:51.367 --> 00:03:53.300
I'd love to give it a try, sure, sure.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:55.323
Anybody out there listening
that has any shows around?

00:03:55.323 --> 00:03:56.257
Just--

00:03:56.257 --> 00:03:57.090
There are plenty.

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:57.923
There are plenty, just
walk around New York

00:03:57.923 --> 00:03:58.756
for like 20 minutes.

00:03:58.756 --> 00:03:59.589
I've heard that, yes.

00:03:59.589 --> 00:04:00.610
Yeah, all right.

00:04:00.610 --> 00:04:02.980
Now, I know that you're
up on current events.

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:04.530
Is there anything you wanna talk about?

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:06.930
Any current events at all,
that you know you, as a frog

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:08.069
would like to comment on?

00:04:08.069 --> 00:04:10.450
Well, you know I try to
be up on current events,

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:12.160
but I've had a little problem recently

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:13.690
because I live in the swamp,

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:15.670
and it's very hard to
have a television there.

00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:18.260
It's kind of an electrical
and water thing,

00:04:18.260 --> 00:04:19.690
so the cable's been out.

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:21.410
You may be able to fill
me in on a few things.

00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:22.243
I don't know.

00:04:22.243 --> 00:04:23.150
No, I couldn't tell you a thing.

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:23.983
I don't watch TV.

00:04:23.983 --> 00:04:24.816
You don't?

00:04:24.816 --> 00:04:25.649
It's a waste of valuable time.

00:04:25.649 --> 00:04:27.230
Well, okay, let's, yeah, yeah.

00:04:27.230 --> 00:04:28.380
I'll go along with that one.

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:29.213
I'll go along with that one.

00:04:29.213 --> 00:04:30.850
All right, so buy yeah,
you're enjoying yourself.

00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:32.890
Everything's fine and you've
had a good time and the album.

00:04:32.890 --> 00:04:34.360
Is there anything else you
want to say about the album?

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:35.770
Well, it was a lot of fun.

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:36.990
It's coming out in a week or so

00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:38.130
and it's got all the Muppets

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:39.902
and we sing with people like,
as you said, Ozzy Osbourne,

00:04:39.902 --> 00:04:41.460
one of my old favorite,

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:44.010
I don't mean old, I didn't
mean that, cut that part.

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:46.300
One of my best friends, Linda Ronstadt.

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:47.133
Oh, very good.

00:04:47.133 --> 00:04:48.290
Yes, I love Linda Ronstadt.

00:04:48.290 --> 00:04:49.710
She's one of my favorite people,

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:51.450
and all those kind of folks,

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:53.440
you know good singers, good songs.

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:54.810
Excellent, well listen,

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:56.528
I wanna wish you the best
of luck with the album.

00:04:56.528 --> 00:04:57.361
Oh, thank you.

00:04:57.361 --> 00:04:58.260
I will ask you, next
time you are on the show,

00:04:58.260 --> 00:04:59.567
would you sit in the chair?

00:04:59.567 --> 00:05:01.000
Ah, I'll see what I can do.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.470
You and Bobcat Goldthwait are the only two

00:05:02.470 --> 00:05:03.360
that have sat up there.

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:04.193
Oh really?

00:05:04.193 --> 00:05:05.140
Oh, at least I'm in good company.

00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:06.551
Yeah, you're in very good company.

00:05:06.551 --> 00:05:07.470
(audience and Conan laugh)

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:08.620
It's a frog thing.

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:09.560
We have to, you know,

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:11.520
you said you look down
on some of your guests?

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:13.677
Well, I just wanted to be up
here at eye level, you know.

00:05:13.677 --> 00:05:14.570
Ah, very nice.

00:05:14.570 --> 00:05:16.571
Well listen, Kermit, thank
you very much for stopping by.

00:05:16.571 --> 00:05:17.404
Well, it's been a pleasure.

00:05:17.404 --> 00:05:19.277
Best of luck with the album,
Kermit the Frog everybody!

00:05:19.277 --> 00:05:20.517
(audience cheers)

00:05:20.517 --> 00:05:21.357
[Conan] Give him a hand!

00:05:21.357 --> 00:05:24.057
(audience cheers)

